{
  "mn15:0.1": "Middle Discourses 15 ",
  "mn15:0.2": "Measuring Up ",
  "mn15:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn15:1.2": "At one time Venerable Mahāmoggallāna was staying in the land of the Bhaggas at Crocodile’s Bellow, in the deer park at Bhesakaḷā’s Wood. ",
  "mn15:1.3": "There Venerable Mahāmoggallāna addressed the mendicants: ",
  "mn15:1.4": "“Reverends, mendicants!” ",
  "mn15:1.5": "“Reverend,” they replied. ",
  "mn15:1.6": "Venerable Mahāmoggallāna said this: ",
  "mn15:2.1": "“Suppose a mendicant invites ",
  "mn15:2.2": "other mendicants to admonish them. But they’re hard to admonish, having qualities that make them hard to admonish. They’re impatient, and don’t take instruction respectfully. So their spiritual companions don’t think it’s worth advising and instructing them, and that individual doesn’t gain their trust. ",
  "mn15:3.1": "And what are the qualities that make them hard to admonish? ",
  "mn15:3.2": "Firstly, a mendicant has corrupt wishes, having fallen under the sway of corrupt wishes. ",
  "mn15:3.3": "",
  "mn15:3.4": "This is a quality that makes them difficult to admonish. ",
  "mn15:3.5": "Furthermore, a mendicant glorifies themselves and puts others down. … ",
  "mn15:3.6": "",
  "mn15:3.7": "",
  "mn15:3.8": "They’re irritable, overcome by anger … ",
  "mn15:3.9": "",
  "mn15:3.10": "",
  "mn15:3.11": "They’re irritable, and acrimonious due to anger … ",
  "mn15:3.12": "",
  "mn15:3.13": "",
  "mn15:3.14": "They’re irritable, and